    <description>ALF-RS-09 (LFRDN-339) FR6: blocks StageName -&gt; Closed Won unless every AF_Payment__c on the Opportunity is verified (Paid / Verified or Keyloop Synced), each has a real attached proof document (ContentDocumentLink - BRD FR6 says &quot;attaching the receipt or deposit document&quot; / &quot;carries an attached payment proof&quot;, not a text reference), and the Invoice Summary balance is zero. Before-save Flow (not the Apex AF_Opportunity_ClosedWonPaymentGate class directly - before-save Flow context cannot call Apex Actions, confirmed against Salesforce&apos;s own Flow documentation) so this enforces on every save path (UI, API, Data Loader, other flows), not just a screen action someone remembers to click. Bulkified deliberately: the ContentDocumentLink lookup for every Payment on the Opportunity runs ONCE before the payment-checking loop (Get_ContentDocumentLinks_For_Payments, filtered by an IN-list built from Get_All_Payments via Loop_Build_PaymentIds), collected into var_PaymentIdsWithFileText (a pipe-delimited string, e.g. |Id1|Id2|) via a separate small loop over the file-link results - Get Records inside the payment-checking loop is a documented Flow anti-pattern that blows the 100-SOQL limit under bulk Opportunity updates. A Decision&apos;s In operator rejects a plain Text variable as the left operand at deploy time (&quot;A condition doesn&apos;t support ... In&quot;) even though the same operator accepts collections fine on the right side of an In filter on a Get Records element - worked around with a CONTAINS() formula against the delimited string instead, which Flow formulas fully support regardless of that Decision-element restriction. Mirrors the exact same dual-verification rule (AF_Status__c = &apos;Paid / Verified&apos; OR AF_IntegrationStatus__c = &apos;Synced&apos;) and file-attachment check that AF_Opportunity_ClosedWonPaymentGate.cls already implements for a callable/testable UI path - if that class&apos;s rule ever changes, this flow must be updated to match, since there is no way to share logic between an Apex class and a before-save Flow.

ALF-RS-11 (LFRDN-341) FR1/FR6 additions: Get_Handover/Handover_Conditions_Met block Closed Won unless the Opportunity&apos;s linked AF_Handover__c has AF_TrafficFormUploaded__c = true (registration) and AF_CustomerSignOff__c = &apos;Physically Signed&apos; (signed delivery note) - read via the Opportunity.AF_Handover__c lookup rather than new Opportunity mirror fields, since AF_HandoverComplete__c/AF_DeliveryConfirmation__c above are already-known unwired manual checkboxes and the new conditions deliberately don&apos;t repeat that gap. Stamp_Close_Date sets CloseDate = TODAY() only on the path where every condition actually passes (FR6: &quot;Closed Won date... based on when the agreed completion conditions are satisfied, not on an earlier sales milestone&quot;), overriding whatever value a rep had typed in earlier.

ALF-RS-11 FR3/FR4/FR5 (payee/NOC, Cheque copy, Bank LPO) were originally enforced only by AF_Opportunity_ClosedWonPaymentGate.cls via the LFRDN-342 AF_Document__mdt engine (AF_DocumentService.areRequiredDocumentsUploaded per Payment) - see LFRDN-682 below for why that changed.

LFRDN-682 (found live 2026-09-22, fixed 2026-09-22): the manual Path close was observed succeeding while AF_Opportunity_ClosedWonPaymentGate.check() on the same record returned allowed=false for a missing typed document (Bank LPO/Signed NOC) - this Flow&apos;s generic file-attached check passed even though the Apex class&apos;s typed-document check would not have. The full LFRDN-342 AF_Document__mdt interpreter is generic/dynamic-SOQL-driven and genuinely can&apos;t be replicated in Flow, but its 5 AF_DocumentCondition__mdt rows for Payment collapse to exactly 3 independent, static rules once read together: Cheque Copy is required when AF_PaymentMethod__c = &apos;Cheque&apos;, Bank LPO when AF_PaymentMethod__c = &apos;Bank Transfer&apos;, and Signed NOC when AF_NOCRecorded__c = true - each fires or doesn&apos;t regardless of the others, so no combinatorial condition-matching engine is actually needed for this one object. Reimplemented those 3 rules declaratively: Get_ContentDocumentLinks_For_Payments (already bulkified per the pattern above) is now also split by ContentDocument.LatestPublishedVersion.AF_FileUpload__c into 3 additional pipe-delimited ID collections (one per document type, mirroring var_PaymentIdsWithFileText&apos;s existing pattern), and Formula_CurrentPaymentHasRequiredTypedDocs checks each Payment against only the type(s) its own method/NOC state actually requires. If AF_DocumentCondition__mdt for Payment is ever restructured beyond these 3 independent rules (e.g. a document required by a genuine AND of two conditions that isn&apos;t already covered by one of the 5 existing rows), this formula must be rebuilt to match - it is not a general interpreter, only a correct model of the specific 5 rows that exist today.

LFRDN-687 (fixed 2026-09-22): Block_Closed_Won was previously a single custom error reused by all four failure branches (no invoice, balance not zero, handover incomplete, unverified/unproofed payment), so every refusal showed the same payment-focused message even when payments were the one thing already correct. Split into five error elements (Block_Closed_Won_No_Invoice, _Balance, _Handover, _Unverified_Payment, _Missing_Proof), one per branch, each naming the actual unmet condition - matching the per-condition messages AF_Opportunity_ClosedWonPaymentGate.cls already produces on the automatic path.</description>
    <environments>Default</environments>
    <formulas>
        <name>Formula_CurrentPaymentHasFile</name>
        <dataType>Boolean</dataType>
        <expression>CONTAINS({!var_PaymentIdsWithFileText}, &quot;|&quot; &amp; {!var_CurrentPaymentId} &amp; &quot;|&quot;)</expression>
    </formulas>
    <formulas>
        <description>LFRDN-682: mirrors the 5 AF_DocumentCondition__mdt Payment rows (collapsed to their 3 independent underlying rules, since the mdt rows are just every combination of them) - Cheque Copy required when PaymentMethod=Cheque, Bank LPO required when PaymentMethod=Bank Transfer, Signed NOC required when NOCRecorded=true. Each clause short-circuits to true when its own condition doesn&apos;t apply, so a payment only needs the document types it actually triggers.</description>
        <name>Formula_CurrentPaymentHasRequiredTypedDocs</name>
        <dataType>Boolean</dataType>
        <expression>AND(
    OR(
        NOT(TEXT({!Loop_All_Payments.AF_PaymentMethod__c}) = &quot;Cheque&quot;),
        CONTAINS({!var_PaymentIdsWithChequeCopyText}, &quot;|&quot; &amp; {!Loop_All_Payments.Id} &amp; &quot;|&quot;)
    ),
    OR(
        NOT(TEXT({!Loop_All_Payments.AF_PaymentMethod__c}) = &quot;Bank Transfer&quot;),
        CONTAINS({!var_PaymentIdsWithBankLPOText}, &quot;|&quot; &amp; {!Loop_All_Payments.Id} &amp; &quot;|&quot;)
    ),
    OR(
        NOT({!Loop_All_Payments.AF_NOCRecorded__c}),
        CONTAINS({!var_PaymentIdsWithSignedNOCText}, &quot;|&quot; &amp; {!Loop_All_Payments.Id} &amp; &quot;|&quot;)
    )
)</expression>
    </formulas>
